# Checkpoint pointer files (these must be tracked)
# These files are committed to git and form the verification chain

# Superseded generation objects
# Objects listed in deleted_paths of current.json/previous.json are superseded
# and should not be tracked. The active roots are added selectively via
# scripts/commit-checkpoint.sh

# NOTE: We do NOT use gen-*.jsonl here because that would ignore the active
# roots we need to track. Instead, superseded objects are simply never added
# to git in the first place.
